  "//": "Not embedded and never loaded at runtime (see uStrings.pas -- locale 'en' always returns each call site's own inline default, so this file can never itself drift out of sync). This is the authoring template: every key a translator needs, next to its current English text, to build strings/<locale>.json from. Keep it in sync with the T()/TDialog() call sites as they're added, so a translator always has the full list.",
  "//dialogs_note": "Ids intentionally omitted here (and so untranslated) are either (a) always overwritten at runtime via DialogSetLabelText/DialogSetTitle before the dialog is shown -- translating their JSON default would never be seen -- or (b) multi-column list headers (assocHeader, header in colorcoding/joblist/keymap, hotlistHeader, sshHeader, wsHeader) whose fixed-width padding lines up with data rows the Pascal code positions independently; translating those needs a matching change to the row-rendering offsets, not just text, so it's left as follow-up work.",

